\title{Booleans in Disco}
\date{2026-01-28T20:26:09Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{In [[0027]], the type \tt{Bool} has two values, \tt{T} and \tt{F} (which can also be written \tt{True} and \tt{False}, or \tt{true} and \tt{false}):
\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> :type T
T : Bool
Disco> :type F
F : Bool
Disco> true
T
Disco> False
F<<<
}

\p{One way we can create \tt{Bool} values in Disco is using \em{comparison operators}:
\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> 3 < 9
T
Disco> 3 > 9
F
Disco> 6 <= 7
T
Disco> 6 >= 7
F
Disco> 5 == 5
T
Disco> 6 /= 5
T<<<
}
